// chgrp.fern — GNU-compatible `chgrp`.
//
//   chgrp [OPTION]... GROUP FILE...
//   chgrp [OPTION]... --reference=RFILE FILE...
//
// `chown` with the user half taken away. The options, the walk, the symlink
// rules and every message are the same code — `chown.fern`'s `run` — told to
// read its operand as a group and to say "group of" where the other says
// "ownership of".
//
// Two things are NOT symmetrical, and both are GNU's:
//
//   - the operand is ONE group token, colons and dots included, so
//     `chgrp a:b f` is `invalid group: 'a:b'` rather than a split;
//   - `--from=` is still the FULL `[USER][:[GROUP]]` spec, so
//     `chgrp --from=staff` is `invalid user: 'staff'` and `--from=:staff` is
//     what was meant.
import "./chown";

function main(): i32 {
  return chown.run(args(), true, "chgrp");
}
